WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.500
[laughing awkwardly] What a weird beginning for a video that's titled this.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.260
Hi guys, my name is Grace Helbig. If you did not know, now you know and your life is different now

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:17.520
I could not think of a video idea that I wanted to post today, and I realized a lot of the reason I couldn't just

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.810
allow myself to think...

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:26.849
clearly was because I was feeling a little depressed, and spoiler alert this happens to me kind of frequently and as an adult I've talked to some

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:30.900
professionals and I can identify it and it's okay, and everything's fine

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:37.340
and it's normal but I thought, "Hey, why don't we just embrace this and make this the video?"

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.160
I've been managing my own

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.820
anxiety and whatever

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:46.440
feelings for years and years now, so I thought hey let's use this video as

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:51.149
a way to show you guys things I've learned over the years that helped me...

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.000
calm the bad

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.930
I like to engage in passive creative activities. For me that's cooking, but then I realize that I'm not cooking

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:06.299
I'm just using this activity to avoid my inbox and unanswered calls from family members and loved ones, and then I just--

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:15.039
Another tactic I use is watching reality television. I love it. I think it's so dumb and so fun, until I realize that perhaps

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:21.040
I'm using it as a tool to watch people that I subconsciously think are in deeper pain than I am and then I just--

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:30.020
Another major tactic is playing with my dog who gives me nothing but pure love energy

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.860
because she thinks that her job is just to love me and it's

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:38.699
absolutely amazing, until I realized that I voluntarily linked myself up with something I would likely outlive and then I just--

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.220
Sometimes I do my hair and makeup to feel better

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:47.600
and then I realize the fleeting side of vanity because my body is a vessel for my personality,

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:54.320
it doesn't actually represent who I am or what legacy I want to leave because it will decline rapidly and then I just--

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.820
Sometimes I like to read very intellectually inspiring books

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:02.720
that have been recommended on Instagram before I realize that the person that recommended this on Instagram and also myself are just

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:08.600
trying to seem cool by association rather than actually taking into thought any of the intellectual, inspiring material inside the book, and then I just--

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:14.280
Exercise is my number one go-to for any sort of anxiety that I am experiencing

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:20.700
until I realize that I'm alone with my thoughts, and what am I actually running from, metaphorically not physically? And then I just--

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.040
Well there you go. There are a few ways that

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:28.530
I manage my personal anxiety and depression. If you liked this video give it a thumbs up. Don't forget to subscribe to my YouTube channel

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:30.530
I make videos Monday, Wednesday, and Friday

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.400
infrequently... unless the demons in the head come out to play.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.340
I don't know.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.580
I think we got that one [snorting laugh].

